      <th>Primary Business Outcomes</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><b>Developer A (Customer)</b></td>
      <td><code>accounts</code>, <code>addresses</code>, <code>cart</code>, <code>checkout</code>, <code>orders</code>, <code>payments</code>, <code>size-recommendations</code></td>
      <td>Customer address CRUD, user-scoped carts, transactional checkout, order snapshots, background unpaid-order expiry worker, simulated mock payments, and rule-based sizing.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><b>Developer B (Staff)</b></td>
      <td><code>catalog</code>, <code>categories</code>, <code>collections</code>, <code>size-guides</code></td>
      <td>Product catalog management, variant SKU uniqueness, category hierarchy, collection bridges (M:N), and size-guide measurement brackets.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><b>Developer C (Inventory)</b></td>
      <td><code>inventory</code>, <code>stock-movements</code>, <code>fulfillment</code>, <code>shipments</code></td>
      <td>SKU balance tracking (<code>on_hand</code>, <code>reserved</code>), row-locked reservation APIs, append-only stock movement logs, order packing, and shipping dispatch.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><b>Developer D (Admin — You)</b></td>
      <td><code>auth</code>, <code>users</code>, <code>roles</code>, <code>audit</code>, <code>analytics</code></td>
      <td>Authentication foundation (JWT + bcrypt), RBAC guards, staff account administration, transactional audit logging, platform operational analytics, and admin seed script.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>5. Request & Response Lifecycle Pipeline</h2>
<p>
Every incoming HTTP request traverses a standardized NestJS middleware, guard, pipe, and interceptor pipeline:
</p>
<ol>
  <li><b>RequestLoggingMiddleware</b>: Mounts before route handlers; generates a unique UUID <code>X-Request-ID</code> header, tracks latency, and logs client requests cleanly.</li>
  <li><b>JwtAuthGuard & Passport Strategy</b>: Validates the Bearer token in the <code>Authorization</code> header; decodes claims and populates <code>req.user</code>.</li>
  <li><b>RolesGuard</b>: Reads role metadata specified by the <code>@Roles(...)</code> decorator and denies access with a safe <code>403 Forbidden</code> if the user lacks the required role.</li>
  <li><b>ValidationPipe</b>: Strips unwhitelisted properties (<code>whitelist: true, forbidNonWhitelisted: true</code>) and returns client-safe <code>400 Bad Request</code> with field-level validation errors.</li>
  <li><b>HttpExceptionFilter</b>: Catches all exceptions (including PostgreSQL error code <code>23505</code> for unique violations) and wraps them into a unified, non-leaking error envelope.</li>
</ol>

<pre>
Standard Success Envelope:
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "OK",
  "data": { ... },
  "meta": {
    "requestId": "6f2d7ea0-6df8-41f5-a28a-493bdaed806d",
    "pagination": { "page": 1, "limit": 20, "total": 100, "totalPages": 5 }
  }
}

Standard Error Envelope:
{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Validation failed",
  "error": {
    "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",
    "details": [{ "field": "email", "message": "email must be an email" }]
  },
  "meta": { "requestId": "6f2d7ea0-6df8-41f5-a28a-493bdaed806d" }
}
</pre>

<h2>6. Critical ACID Database Transactions (Course Requirement M2)</h2>
<p>
The project features two critical transactional workflows that guarantee data consistency and demonstrate advanced TypeORM transaction handling:
</p>

<h3>Scenario 1: High-Concurrency Customer Checkout</h3>
<ol>
  <li>Customer sends <code>POST /api/v1/checkout</code> with an <code>Idempotency-Key</code> header.</li>
  <li>Validates delivery address ownership and cart contents.</li>
  <li>Starts a database transaction via <code>DataSource.transaction()</code>.</li>
  <li>Fetches authoritative prices from the catalog (ignoring client-side prices).</li>
  <li>Acquires <b>pessimistic row locks</b> (<code>SELECT FOR UPDATE</code>) on all variant balance rows.</li>
  <li>Verifies <code>on_hand - reserved &gt;= requested_quantity</code> for each item.</li>
  <li>Increments <code>reserved</code> stock and inserts <code>stock_reservations</code> with an expiration timestamp.</li>
  <li>Inserts the <code>orders</code> row (status: <code>PENDING_PAYMENT</code>) and frozen <code>order_items</code> snapshots.</li>
  <li>Empties the customer's cart and saves an idempotency record.</li>
  <li>Commits the transaction. If two customers simultaneously check out the last remaining item, exactly one succeeds and the other receives <code>409 Conflict</code> (insufficient stock). If any operation fails, all changes roll back immediately.</li>
</ol>

<h3>Scenario 2: Admin Staff Lifecycle & Audit Logging (Your Feature)</h3>
<p>
Whenever an Administrator creates, updates, or deactivates a staff member in <code>UsersService</code>:
</p>
<ol>
  <li>Opens an explicit transaction via <code>this.dataSource.transaction(async manager =&gt; ...)</code>.</li>
  <li>Saves or updates the staff user entity.</li>
  <li>Calls <code>AuditService.record(..., manager)</code> to insert an immutable audit trail entry containing the actor's ID, action code (e.g., <code>STAFF_CREATED</code>, <code>STAFF_UPDATED</code>, <code>STAFF_DEACTIVATED</code>), and JSON snapshots of <code>before</code> and <code>after</code> states.</li>
  <li>Both operations commit simultaneously. If the audit log fails to record, the staff account change is completely rolled back, guaranteeing an unalterable audit trail.</li>
</ol>

<h2>7. Admin Domain Endpoints Reference (Role D)</h2>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Endpoint</th>
      <th>HTTP Method</th>
      <th>Access</th>
      <th>Description</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><code>/api/v1/auth/register</code></td>
      <td>POST</td>
      <td>Public</td>
      <td>Registers a new customer. Role is strictly forced to <code>CUSTOMER</code>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>/api/v1/auth/login</code></td>
      <td>POST</td>
      <td>Public</td>
      <td>Verifies credentials against bcrypt password hashes and issues a JWT Bearer token.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>/api/v1/users/me</code></td>
      <td>GET</td>
      <td>Any Authenticated</td>
      <td>Returns safe user profile (excluding password hash) for the current caller.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>/api/v1/admin/staff</code></td>
      <td>POST</td>
      <td>ADMIN</td>
      <td>Creates a new <code>STAFF</code> or <code>INVENTORY_MANAGER</code> account with an audited record.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>/api/v1/admin/staff</code></td>
      <td>GET</td>
      <td>ADMIN</td>
      <td>Returns paginated list of staff accounts with optional filtering by role and status.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>/api/v1/admin/staff/:id</code></td>
      <td>GET</td>
      <td>ADMIN</td>
      <td>Retrieves detailed profile information for a specific staff member.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>/api/v1/admin/staff/:id</code></td>
      <td>PATCH</td>
      <td>ADMIN</td>
      <td>Updates staff name, role, or status with before/after state capture in audit logs.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>/api/v1/admin/staff/:id</code></td>
      <td>DELETE</td>
      <td>ADMIN</td>
      <td>Deactivates (soft-deletes) staff member by setting status to <code>INACTIVE</code> and writes audit log.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>/api/v1/admin/audit-logs</code></td>
      <td>GET</td>
      <td>ADMIN</td>
      <td>Browses paginated system audit log entries with filter options (by action, entity, actor).</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>/api/v1/admin/analytics/summary</code></td>
      <td>GET</td>
      <td>ADMIN</td>
      <td>Returns high-level platform statistics: user counts by role/status, audit volume, and catalog/order totals.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

